{
  "components": [
    {
      "text": "# Request a credit line increase",
      "type": "text",
      "layout": {
        "row": "Row_heading",
        "columns": null
      },
      "id": "Field_Heading"
    },
    {
      "text": "**This form only starts the case.** Once submitted, the agent fires a no-op request to the credit bureau and then genuinely waits - the bureau's reply does **not** come back through a form. It arrives later as a **webhook call**: open the **credit-line-increase-agent** process definition in Modeler, click the **Wait for bureau report** task, and copy its webhook URL from the **Webhooks** tab (one URL, reused for every case - it correlates by customerId). Then `POST` the bureau's reply to it, e.g.\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST \"<the webhook URL>\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"customerId\": \"<the customerId you entered below>\",\n    \"creditScoreExternal\": 712,\n    \"existingDebtUSD\": 8400,\n    \"bureauFlags\": \"none\"\n  }'\n```\n\nIf you don't send it within the demo SLA window (3 minutes), the agent is told the bureau timed out and may - its own judgment call - ask underwriting ops for a manual decision in Tasklist instead.",
      "type": "text",
      "layout": {
        "row": "Row_webhookNote",
        "columns": null
      },
      "id": "Field_WebhookNote"
    },
    {
      "label": "Customer ID",
      "description": "Used as the correlation key for the bureau's later webhook reply - reuse this exact value in the curl command above.",
      "type": "textfield",
      "layout": {
        "row": "Row_customerId",
        "columns": null
      },
      "id": "Field_CustomerId",
      "key": "customerId",
      "defaultValue": "CUST-70210",
      "validate": {
        "required": true
      }
    },
    {
      "label": "Current credit limit (USD)",
      "type": "number",
      "layout": {
        "row": "Row_currentLimit",
        "columns": null
      },
      "id": "Field_CurrentLimit",
      "key": "currentLimitUSD",
      "defaultValue": 5000,
      "validate": {
        "required": true
      }
    },
    {
      "label": "Requested credit limit (USD)",
      "type": "number",
      "layout": {
        "row": "Row_requestedLimit",
        "columns": null
      },
      "id": "Field_RequestedLimit",
      "key": "requestedLimitUSD",
      "defaultValue": 8000,
      "validate": {
        "required": true
      }
    },
    {
      "label": "Customer tenure (years)",
      "type": "number",
      "layout": {
        "row": "Row_tenure",
        "columns": null
      },
      "id": "Field_Tenure",
      "key": "customerTenureYears",
      "defaultValue": 3,
      "validate": {
        "required": true
      }
    },
    {
      "label": "Late payments in the last 90 days",
      "type": "number",
      "layout": {
        "row": "Row_latePayments",
        "columns": null
      },
      "id": "Field_LatePayments",
      "key": "recentLatePayments90d",
      "defaultValue": 0,
      "validate": {
        "required": true
      }
    },
    {
      "label": "Reason for the request",
      "type": "textarea",
      "layout": {
        "row": "Row_reason",
        "columns": null
      },
      "id": "Field_Reason",
      "key": "requestReason",
      "defaultValue": "Wants headroom for an upcoming home renovation purchase.",
      "validate": {
        "required": true
      }
    }
  ],
  "type": "default",
  "id": "credit-line-request",
  "executionPlatform": "Camunda Cloud",
  "executionPlatformVersion": "8.10.0",
  "exporter": {
    "name": "Camunda Modeler",
    "version": "5.49.0"
  },
  "schemaVersion": 19
}
